# Frontend UI

## Theme (non-negotiable)

- **Follow the existing app theme.** Reuse colors, type, spacing, radii, and components from CSS variables already in the product.
- **Do not invent a theme** (new palette, new font stack, new "AI SaaS" look) when adding screens.
- If tokens already exist, import or mirror them. If there is no UI yet, keep it plain.
- When unsure, ask or inspect existing UI source. Never "improve" branding in a drive-by.

## Anti-AI UI structures

Avoid default agent UI kits:

- Purple / indigo gradients on white
- Glow shadows, glassmorphism, neon accents
- Pill chip rows, badge clusters, icon-stat strips in the hero
- Generic Inter/Roboto/Arial stacks when the app already sets fonts
- Card grids that add chrome without interaction need
- Fake dashboards, empty "insights" widgets, decorative charts

## Layout discipline

- One job per section. One primary CTA.
- Prefer product flows (quote → pay → status) over marketing ornament on app screens.
- Status UI must separate **Bitcoin received** from **RWF delivered**.
- Mobile-first; match existing breakpoints and nav patterns.

## Copy in UI

Obey `voice-and-copy` (no em dashes, sentence case, no AI filler). Labels stay short and literal.
